00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.320
Hi everyone, my name is Briana Frank&nbsp;
and I'm with the IBM Cloud team.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.040
Let's talk about IBM Cloud Satellite.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:13.520
Today, many enterprises are benefiting from using&nbsp;
public cloud to build and run their applications.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:21.680
Being able to consume IT as a service, through&nbsp;
APIs, at scale, and as needed has transformed how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:27.280
applications are built. Public Cloud enabled&nbsp;
companies to innovate in new, faster ways.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.560
But the reality is only somewhere between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:37.520
5% and 20% of enterprise workloads have moved&nbsp;
to the cloud. That first wave of applications&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.520
were focused mostly on new workloads&nbsp;
or workloads that can easily relocate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:48.880
Many applications have requirements around&nbsp;
security, compliance, latency, regulation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:55.200
and performance that mean those workloads can't&nbsp;
easily move into a public cloud.&nbsp;Enterprises need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.320
an ability to gain the benefits of public cloud&nbsp;
anywhere they need their applications to run.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.280
What would help these enterprises is&nbsp;
something called Distributed Cloud.&nbsp;

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:10.400
Distributed cloud is a new cloud computing&nbsp;
model that extends public cloud services&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.280
to any location. This means companies&nbsp;
can now run not only in their primary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.920
cloud provider's infrastructure but on&nbsp;
premises, in other cloud providers',&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:25.520
in third party data centers or colocation&nbsp;
centers, or at the edge - in factories,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:31.280
distribution centers, stores, hospitals&nbsp;
and ports - with everything managed from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:36.640
single control plane. IBM Cloud Satellite is&nbsp;
our new distributed cloud capability.&nbsp;With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:42.080
Satellite you can take advantage of the&nbsp;
catalog of services from IBM cloud with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:47.440
industry optimized security and compliance&nbsp;
and leading AI capabilities anywhere you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:54.480
need it. All with a common API, user experience,&nbsp;
management dashboard and user consumption model.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:00.720
To see how IBM Cloud Satellite works, let’s&nbsp;
take a look at a couple of real-world examples.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.240
We’ll start with the financial services&nbsp;
industry.&nbsp; On the surface, the financial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:11.200
services industry might seem like it's all about&nbsp;
money, but it's really all about technology.&nbsp;In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.360
order to compete, financial institutions&nbsp;
need to create exceptional user experiences.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.840
To do that, they leverage AI and trading&nbsp;
algorithms to stay ahead of the market.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:27.440
To be competitive financial services clients&nbsp;
need to iterate quickly and leverage cloud-native&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:34.160
tools and best practices. However, the financial&nbsp;
industry is heavily regulated. So, they need to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:39.360
be able to keep that data secure and compliant&nbsp;
- which often means there are restrictions on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:44.960
where that data can live. IBM Cloud Satellite&nbsp;
can help solve this conflict.&nbsp; These financial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:50.480
services companies can now extend public cloud&nbsp;
services in their data centers, allowing them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:55.360
to leverage cloud native best practices and meet&nbsp;
their security and compliance obligations, all at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:01.200
the same time. So, Satellite enables you to take&nbsp;
advantage of a public cloud consumption model,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.520
but in many different locations - and you don't&nbsp;
have to be an expert in running these software&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:11.040
stacks to run them outside of the public&nbsp;
cloud. Let's take a look at another example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.600
this time in the construction&nbsp;
industry, where worker safety is key.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:20.560
One of our clients is leveraging distributed&nbsp;
analytics to keep workers safe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.160
In this scenario, you might have a business, or&nbsp;
an office building that is under construction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.720
and you need to be able to leverage video&nbsp;
analytics to tell if someone is wearing a hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:35.600
hat or not - and warn them before they move into&nbsp;
a potentially dangerous area of that building.&nbsp;

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.080
They want to use video analytics to&nbsp;
automatically detect this situation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:45.840
but latency could be a real problem - if you&nbsp;
warn someone too late they could be injured.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:49.280
So, let's take a look at how&nbsp;
this scenario might work.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:55.280
To solve this safety problem, you need to be able&nbsp;
to analyze video data from many cameras all over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.160
the office building, but it's impractical to send&nbsp;
all of that data back to the cloud to be processed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.440
remotely.&nbsp;It would be better if the video&nbsp;
processing happened close to the actual device.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:10.720
Traditionally, that would require you to install&nbsp;
servers and software and manage them on-prem.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.600
With IBM Cloud Satellite, we can extend&nbsp;
the public cloud into the office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:20.400
so we can leverage cloud services to run&nbsp;
this application close to the device - and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:25.040
that's critical in ensuring that we can&nbsp;
reduce latency and effectively warn someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.760
before they enter a dangerous&nbsp;
area.That same client in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:34.800
worker safety scenario had to adjust to&nbsp;
challenges brought by the Covid pandemic.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:40.080
They were able to quickly iterate on&nbsp;
their application and modify the use-case.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.560
Now, instead of warning workers about&nbsp;
wearing hard hats, they can make sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:48.240
that workers are wearing masks and ensure&nbsp;
that the masks are being worn correctly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:54.480
They can even leverage thermal devices to&nbsp;
take temperatures. With IBM Cloud Satellite,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:59.440
you can quickly address unforeseen challenges,&nbsp;
leverage cloud benefits in any location,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:05.920
and innovate quickly. Anytime. Anywhere. thank you&nbsp;
for watching if you have questions please drop us&nbsp;&nbsp;

